Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||07-30-2001||04:02 PM||||My dad Just got back from the Chicago Corvair International convention. He won the Street mod class by a margin of 2 seconds and beat a lot of the Competition class cars<P>Not a bad 60th birthday present considering most of the field was 25+ years younger than he is.<P>Car is a 66 Corsa , 140 engine , built heads 11.1 compression , tripple weber carbs with manifolds modified to accept them. HEaders MSD 6al , front mount oil cooler , Lunati Cam , 3.55 gears , close ratio 4spd. balanced blueprinted ect. Duralight race wheels , Toyo RA1's redlines at 7500+ RPM.<P>Here are some pics:<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/View_18.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/View2_4.jpg"> <P>I was suppose to go to the convention , but was detained with school work.<P>JM<BR>||||reg||1
